  note right of PendingPayment
    PendingPayment - entry / hold crabs on the batch capacity (PreOrderHold «planned»)
    «planned» precondition of start → PendingPayment - batch Funding, crab count (or kg) ≥ the minimum order quantity, address within the farm's delivery radius, crabs left in the batch's PreOrderQuota
    «planned» on PendingPayment → DepositPaid - PreOrderHold Converted
    «planned» on PendingPayment → Cancelled - also at funding close when the batch does not open (case d - nothing is lost)
    «planned» (UC55 Cancel Bulk Pre-order, UC54 Forfeit Deposit, Sequence 4.58) - (a) a Customer who cancels after paying the deposit while the batch is Funding goes to Cancelled and the deposit is kept, it is forfeited if the batch opens, and a cancel after the batch opened (Confirmed) is forfeited at once, (b) if the batch does not open, every paid deposit is refunded, including those of cancelled orders, (c) refusing the delivery or not paying the balance forfeits the deposit and the crabs are resold through an InvoicedSale (ForfeitResale, Figure 4.18), (d) cancelling before paying the deposit (PendingPayment) costs nothing.
    «planned» v1.4 - order_type BulkPreOrder by crab count (or kg) from a minimum quantity while the batch is Funding (no listing), price per kg locked at funding, delivery within the farm radius, the order QR code is issued when the Operator prepares the delivery note, deliver records weighedKg (live crabs the Customer accepts, dead or spoiled crabs left out) and transitLossKg (recorded only) and issues the balance QR, the balance payment moves the order to Delivered and issues its Invoice, receive then only records received_at (Sequence 4.57), a forfeited deposit becomes RevenueLine ForfeitedDeposit (counted once).
  end note
  note right of Confirmed
    Confirmed is «planned» (Register v1.4, not in code)
    «planned» Confirmed → Packed - prepare delivery note (Operator) [crabs of harvested boxes assigned] / order QR code issued
    «planned» Confirmed → Forfeited - cancel (Customer or Investor) [batch opened] / deposit forfeited - RevenueLine ForfeitedDeposit
  end note
  note right of Refunded
    Refunded is «planned» (Register v1.4, not in code)
  end note
  note right of Forfeited
    Forfeited is «planned» (Register v1.4, not in code)
  end note
  note right of DepositPaid
    «planned» DepositPaid → Confirmed - batch opens (funding close job)
    «planned» DepositPaid → Cancelled - cancel (Customer or Investor) [batch still Funding] / deposit kept until funding close, crab hold released
    «planned» DepositPaid → Refunded - batch Cancelled (funding close job) / Refund instruction for the deposit
  end note
  note right of Cancelled
    «planned» Cancelled → Refunded - batch Cancelled (funding close job) [deposit paid] / Refund instruction for the deposit
    «planned» Cancelled → Forfeited - batch opens (funding close job) [deposit paid] / deposit forfeited - RevenueLine ForfeitedDeposit
    «planned» on Cancelled → end - [no deposit paid]
  end note
  note right of Shipping
    «planned» Shipping → Shipping - deliver - record weighedKg and transitLossKg (Operator) / balance QR = weighedKg × price per kg − deposit, if negative, refund the difference
    «planned» on Shipping → Delivered - v1.4 - on the balance webhook [amount = balance] / paid_at, Invoice issued
    «planned» Shipping → Forfeited - refuse delivery or not pay the balance (Customer) / deposit forfeited, balance QR Cancelled, crabs back to stock for an InvoicedSale (saleReason ForfeitResale)
  end note
  note right of Delivered
    «planned» on Delivered → Completed - RevenueLine DeliveredOrder
  end note
  %% Created by place bulk pre-order (Customer or Investor) only if: the user is not the batch's Operator or one of its members; enough crabs left on the batch capacity (no overselling); «planned» batch Funding, crab count (or kg) ≥ the minimum order quantity, address within the farm's delivery radius, crabs left in the batch's PreOrderQuota (UC27).
  %% Deposit rules «planned» (UC55 Cancel Bulk Pre-order, UC54 Forfeit Deposit, Sequence 4.58): (a) a Customer who cancels after paying the deposit while the batch is Funding goes to Cancelled and the deposit is kept; it is forfeited if the batch opens, and a cancel after the batch opened (Confirmed) is forfeited at once; (b) if the batch does not open, every paid deposit is refunded, including those of cancelled orders; (c) refusing the delivery or not paying the balance forfeits the deposit and the crabs are resold through an InvoicedSale (ForfeitResale, Figure 4.18); (d) cancelling before paying the deposit (PendingPayment) costs nothing.
  %% «planned» v1.4: order_type BulkPreOrder by crab count (or kg) from a minimum quantity while the batch is Funding (no listing); price per kg locked at funding; delivery within the farm radius; the order QR code is issued when the Operator prepares the delivery note; deliver records weighedKg (live crabs the Customer accepts, dead or spoiled crabs left out) and transitLossKg (recorded only) and issues the balance QR; the balance payment moves the order to Delivered and issues its Invoice, receive then only records received_at (Sequence 4.57); a forfeited deposit becomes RevenueLine ForfeitedDeposit (counted once).
  %% Today in code (removed in v1.4, not drawn): order_type PreOrder from a Published listing while the batch is InProduction, by kg; the balance is issued when the batch is Harvesting and paid before packing (DepositPaid → Paid, the Paid value of ck_sales_order_status, also used by retail checkout); packing scans crab tags (Paid → Packed). Gaps: DepositPaid never expires and cannot be cancelled (422 order.cannot_cancel); forfeited pre-order deposits are not in v_batch_actual_revenue. An active complaint (Figure 4.19) blocks completion and returns.
